WEBVTT

00:08:29.484 --> 00:08:30.642
And that's more limited.

00:08:30.666 --> 00:08:34.912
Very few animals, I think elephants
and apes, can do that kind of thing.

00:08:36.511 --> 00:08:37.873
So synchronization,

00:08:37.897 --> 00:08:40.040
which is part of that whole
empathy mechanism,

00:08:40.064 --> 00:08:42.319
is a very old one in the animal kingdom.

00:08:42.343 --> 00:08:45.584
In humans, of course,
we can study that with yawn contagion.

00:08:45.608 --> 00:08:47.426
Humans yawn when others yawn.

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:49.233
And it's related to empathy.

00:08:49.257 --> 00:08:51.392
It activates the same areas in the brain.

00:08:51.416 --> 00:08:54.137
Also, we know that people
who have a lot of yawn contagion

00:08:54.161 --> 00:08:55.314
are highly empathic.

00:08:55.338 --> 00:08:58.513
People who have problems with empathy,
such as autistic children,

00:08:58.537 --> 00:09:00.029
they don't have yawn contagion.